{#
  The restore drill's state: the rotation, retry and seen stamps, one key each (H2.3c writes
  them). Rendered empty here. The two annotations below are the reason it is a template of its
  own.

  ssa: IfNotPresent makes Flux create the object once and never revert the drill's writes to its
  data. Without it, every reconcile would empty the keys.

  prune: disabled keeps the object when a render drops it. The tag prunes like any per-tag
  Kustomization, and a revert or a render bug that dropped this ConfigMap would delete state no
  render can restore. Contract C3 exempts it by name (*Prune exemptions*).

  The namespace is `longhorn_drill_namespace`. No Namespace object renders here, because a second
  writer of `homelab` beside ansible/deploy.yml is what C4 forbids.
#}
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: longhorn-restore-drill-stamps
  namespace: {{ longhorn_drill_namespace }}
  annotations:
    kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/ssa: IfNotPresent
    kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/prune: disabled
